[2026-11-02] [orchestrator] [#3] Data model locked: rooms/room_members/tokens/characters; token x/y stored on the token row (board reconstructed by querying rows, ephemeral drags over Socket.IO) — not a denormalized room-state blob. room_members holds per-room role so a user can DM one room and play another. UNIQUE(room_id,user_id) on room_members.
[2026-11-02] [orchestrator] [#3] One character per player per room, DMs own many (NPC cards) — enforced by a BEFORE INSERT/UPDATE trigger (rule depends on role in room_members, which isn't on the characters row, so UNIQUE can't express it).
[2026-11-02] [orchestrator] [#3] Room passwords hashed/verified in Postgres via pgcrypto (crypt/gen_salt), never client-side or in the Socket.IO server (per User Flow #3). Room create/join via SECURITY DEFINER RPCs (create_room, join_room); rooms table is members-only (no public read) to avoid leaking password_hash/room list and to solve the join chicken-and-egg.
[2026-11-02] [orchestrator] [#3] Guarded writes via dedicated RPCs (chosen over triggers): move_token (x/y only, token assigned to caller or DM) and update_character (hp/notes only, own card). Players have NO direct UPDATE policy on tokens/characters; DM gets direct UPDATE. RLS uses SECURITY DEFINER helpers is_room_member/is_room_dm (owned by postgres => bypass RLS, no recursion).
